{"id":"thebez","name":"Thebez","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:thebez"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Thebez","text":"Brightness, a place some 11 miles north-east of Shechem, on the road to Scythopolis, the modern Tabas. Abimelech led his army against this place, because of its participation in the conspiracy of the men of Shechem; but as he drew near to the strong tower to which its inhabitants had fled for safety, and was about to set fire to it, a woman cast a fragment of millstone at him, and “all to brake his skull” i.e., “altogether brake,” etc. His armourbearer thereupon “thrust him through, and he died” (Judg. 9:50-55)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H802","lemma":"אִשָּׁה","xlit":"ʼishshâh","gloss":"a woman","kjv":"ess, each, every, female","count":4,"share":0.5},{"strong":"H4191","lemma":"מוּת","xlit":"mûwth","gloss":"to die","kjv":"at all, crying, dead, death","count":3,"share":0.38}],"verses":["Judg.9.51","Judg.9.53","Judg.9.54","2Sam.11.21","Judg.9.50","Judg.9.52","Judg.9.55","Judg.9.56"],"related":[{"id":"abihail","type":"lexical","strong":"H802","why":"both lead with אִשָּׁה (H802)"},{"id":"abijah","type":"lexical","strong":"H802","why":"both lead with אִשָּׁה (H802)"},{"id":"adah","type":"lexical","strong":"H802","why":"both lead with אִשָּׁה (H802)"},{"id":"adultery","type":"lexical","strong":"H802","why":"both lead with אִשָּׁה (H802)"},{"id":"ahinoam","type":"lexical","strong":"H802","why":"both lead with אִשָּׁה (H802)"},{"id":"alliance-and-society-with-the-enemies-of-god","type":"lexical","strong":"H802","why":"both lead with אִשָּׁה (H802)"},{"id":"amnesty","type":"lexical","strong":"H4191","why":"both lead with מוּת (H4191)"},{"id":"arbitration","type":"lexical","strong":"H4191","why":"both lead with מוּת (H4191)"},{"id":"baal-hanan","type":"lexical","strong":"H4191","why":"both lead with מוּת (H4191)"},{"id":"dead-people","type":"lexical","strong":"H4191","why":"both lead with מוּת (H4191)"},{"id":"dead"